@startuml projects-design
!include _style.puml
title Playground Projects: ports and adapters (planned, not built)
' palette: boundary=blue · service=green · domain=amber · port=lavender · adapter/infra=gray
' PLANNED, NOT BUILT: every box on this page. Written from decisions 13 and 14, before any code (apps/api/app/projects/).
' Same shape as access-design.puml: domain/ is pure, ports.py holds the ports, service.py the use cases,
' adapters/ the SQL one. main.py (the composition root) builds the Caller and wires the three adapters.
' It is the design shared by UC-P1, UC-P2 and UC-P3.
' Projects imports neither Access nor Audit. The AccountStatus adapter and the AuditLog adapter are wired in the
' composition root to Access (BC-ACCESS) and Audit (BC-AUDIT), so no context imports another (decision 14).
' Not drawn: the route functions, and the full check (token, account found, not deactivated, not pending) that runs
' in main.py before a Caller exists. HTTP statuses are mapped there: ProjectNotFound 404, NotAnAdministrator 403,
' MemberNotEligible and InvalidProjectName 422.
' Everything is under the Project aggregate: files, endpoints and evaluations are other contexts, not drawn.

top to bottom direction

class "«value object»\nCaller" as CAL #D5E8D4 {
  account_id
  is_administrator
}

class "«root entity»\nProject" as PRJ #FFE6CC {
  id
  name : ProjectName
  created
  created_by
  memberships
}

class "«entity»\nMembership" as MEM #FFF2CC {
  account_id
  added
  added_by
}

class "«value object»\nProjectName" as NAM #D5E8D4 {
  trimmed, 1 to 100
}

class "«domain rules»\nProjectRules" as RUL #FFE6CC {
  +may_see(caller, project)
  +may_change_members(caller)
}

class "«domain errors»\nProjectErrors" as ERR #FFE6CC {
  ProjectNotFound
  NotAnAdministrator
  MemberNotEligible
  InvalidProjectName
}

class "«service»\nProjectsService" as SVC #E7F4EA {
  +create(caller, name, first_members)
  +add_member(caller, project_id, account_id)
  +remove_member(caller, project_id, account_id)
  +list_for(caller)
  +open(caller, project_id)
}

class "«port»\nProject-\nRepository" as PPR #EEE7F7 {
  +get(project_id)
  +add(project)
  +save(project)
  +list_all()
  +list_for_member(account_id)
}
class "«port»\nAccountStatus" as PAS #EEE7F7 {
  +active_among(account_ids)
}
class "«port»\nAuditLog" as PAL #EEE7F7 {
  +record(entry)
}

class "«adapter»\nSqlProjects" as SQL #EEE7F7
class "«adapter»\nAccountStatus-\nAdapter" as ASA #EEE7F7
class "«adapter»\nAuditLog-\nAdapter" as ALA #EEE7F7

class "API database\n(PostgreSQL,\nAmazon RDS)" as DB #ECECEC
class "Access\n(BC-ACCESS)" as ACC #ECECEC
class "Audit\n(BC-AUDIT)" as AUD #ECECEC

PRJ *-- MEM
PRJ --> NAM
SVC ..> RUL : asks
SVC ..> PRJ
RUL ..> ERR
RUL ..> CAL
SVC ..> CAL : receives
SVC --> PPR
SVC --> PAS
SVC --> PAL
PPR <|.. SQL
PAS <|.. ASA
PAL <|.. ALA
SQL --> DB
ASA ..> ACC : composition root
ALA ..> AUD : composition root

CAL -[hidden]right-> NAM
PRJ -[hidden]right-> MEM
RUL -[hidden]right-> ERR
PPR -[hidden]right-> PAS
PAS -[hidden]right-> PAL
SQL -[hidden]right-> ASA
ASA -[hidden]right-> ALA
DB -[hidden]right-> ACC
ACC -[hidden]right-> AUD
CAL -[hidden]down-> PRJ
PRJ -[hidden]down-> RUL
RUL -[hidden]down-> SVC

note bottom of AUD
  The Caller is built by main.py after the full check.
  Projects never looks a role up.
  SqlProjects and the audit write share one database
  session: the change and its entry are one transaction.
end note
@enduml
